{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLNUdNtGvFvvF5mC5UpG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UrsKLyLVReziAQj8XXxRWt","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","query":"glob","perPage":20},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":563,"cache_read_input_tokens":12746,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":563},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66f1d2b8-3a6c-4f35-8b06-0c1f861e8aaf","uuid":"f84f8cd9-e598-41ea-a41c-3e6a9406d9a4","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:42:50.003Z","request_id":"req_011CgLNUd2oEfcnKHJi4uZaD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UrsKLyLVReziAQj8XXxRWt":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","query":"glob","perPage":20}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UrsKLyLVReziAQj8XXxRWt","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UrsKLyLVReziAQj8XXxRWt","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"0803b6ebda4a7acf26659df193707d8ad8d68c61\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T12:59:36+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-6026: Prefetch the vitals charts and keep their height while they load (#3727)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Prefetch the vitals charts and keep their height while they load\\n\\nThe vitals and biometrics widgets now start loading their chart code when\\nsomeone hovers over or focuses the table/chart switcher. By the time they\\nclick, the chart chunk is usually ready and the chart renders without a\\nloading state.\\n\\nWhen the chunk isn't ready yet, the fallback is now a SkeletonPlaceholder\\nthe same height as the rendered chart view (466px plus margins) instead of\\na one-line InlineLoading. The spinner shrank the card to a single line and\\npulled the widgets below it up, then pushed them back down when the chart\\nrendered. The skeleton keeps the card at its final height. It keeps\\nrole=\\\"progressbar\\\" and a \\\"Loading\\\" label for screen readers.\\n\\n* Ignore failed chart prefetches\\n\\nThe hover and focus handlers returned the import promise, so a failed\\nchunk download on hover became an unhandled rejection, and O3's global\\nhandler showed an error toast before anyone opened the chart view.\\n\\nThe handlers now call a prefetch wrapper that ignores the failure.\\nReact.lazy still uses the uncaught loader, so opening the chart view\\nretries the download, and a failure there still reaches an error\\nboundary.\\n\\n* Test the chart prefetch in the vitals and biometrics widgets\\n\\nEach widget gets two tests: hovering the table/chart switcher starts\\nloading the chart module, and a failed prefetch leaves the table in\\nplace without an unhandled rejection. Vitest fails the run on an\\nunhandled rejection, so removing the prefetch's catch fails the suite.\\n\\nThe tests mock the chart module with vi.doMock and import a fresh copy\\nof the widget after vi.resetModules, so each test starts with its own\\nReact.lazy state and a chart module that hasn't been imported yet.\\n\\n---------\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"502b0072964465322124ab769a896c3f09aea226\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T18:38:48-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Patient chart shouldn't generate global CSS rules (#3634)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5ba5b70a72d0a60d3dfa6136efe8237ce118d80b\",\"date\":\"2026-06-30T08:26:53+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) Patch OWASP-reported minimatch vulnerabilities (#3433)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Upgrades three pinned minimatch versions to patched releases to fix\\nGHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74, GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26, and GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj\\n(all High severity, 3 CVEs × 3 affected versions = 9 total findings):\\n\\n- minimatch 3.1.2 → 3.1.5  (^3.x requests, e.g. glob, ignore)\\n- minimatch 5.1.0 → 5.1.9  (^5.x requests)\\n- minimatch 9.0.5 → 9.0.9  (^9.x requests)\\n\\nEach upgrade stays within its major version so API compatibility\\nwith dependents is preserved.\",\"authorName\":\"Jayasanka Weerasinghe\",\"authorEmail\":\"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e359da592c220eecde4552ad213e4bc2cdd8e195\",\"date\":\"2025-07-04T09:41:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades (#2554)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades\\n\\nThis PR addresses performance bottlenecks in visit and encounter data management by replacing global revalidation with more targeted cache invalidation.\\n\\nPresently, the global `mutateVisit()` revalidation function triggers 13+ unnecessary network requests per operation, and all visit-related components are revalidated even when only specific data changed.\\n\\nThis approach:\\n\\n- Replaces the global `mutateVisit()` with targeted SWR cache invalidation to reduce 13+ revalidation requests to 1 per operation.\\n- Moves revalidation utilities from the chart app to `@openmrs/esm-patient-common-lib` for better reusability.\\n- Creates multiple utility functions for surgical cache invalidation:\\n  - `invalidateVisitHistory()` - Only invalidates visit history table data\\n  - `invalidatePatientEncounters()` - Only invalidates encounter data\\n  - `invalidateVisitAndEncounterData()` - Combines both for operations affecting both\\n  - `useOptimisticVisitMutations()` - Hook for optimistic updates without network requests\\n- Fixes the encounter table cache invalidation regex to handle flexible URL parameter order.\\n- Updates all visit/encounter operations to use surgical cache targeting:\\n  - Visit creation/editing (`visit-form.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - Visit deletion/restoration (`useDeleteVisit.hook.tsx`)\\n  - Encounter deletion (`encounters-table.component.tsx`)\\n  - Form submissions (`form-entry.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - Visit note creation (`visit-notes-form.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - Order basket operations (`order-basket.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - Vitals/biometrics forms (`vitals-biometrics-form.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - End visit dialog (`end-visit-dialog.component.tsx`)\\n- Preserves current visit component performance by avoiding unnecessary revalidation.\\n- Ensures the `AllEncountersTable` updates correctly after form submissions and other encounter operations.\\n\\nThis eliminates the performance issue where visit CRUD operations triggered excessive network requests returning 304 responses, while maintaining proper data synchronization across all visit and encounter tables.\\n\\n* Make some tweaks and add test coverage\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0458aeea04bfa22b7aa6971a138d90c596232e1c\",\"date\":\"2024-09-05T16:32:39+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Temporarily remove global E2E test timeout\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a8c867fc9ade074fabf84ebcfc7b26f10869dc7b\",\"date\":\"2024-04-06T01:14:40+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Fix Prettier glob patterns\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b3af1a452d58079342c879e09a970b2053f5c46c\",\"date\":\"2024-01-23T22:27:40+02:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-2752: Encounter view UI fixes for RTL languages (#1596)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-2752: encounter view RTL alignment fix\\r\\n\\r\\n* (fix) O3-2752: remove global overrides\\r\\n\\r\\n---------\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Andrey Y <andrey.yakubyshyn@med.me>\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"elimm\",\"authorEmail\":\"elimm@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0a8ebba37f0fc01ba2cd066d45c11a01ae462ade\",\"date\":\"2024-01-10T22:29:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"(refactor) Set global testTimeout in Jest config (#1573)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (refactor) Set global testTimeout in Jest config\\r\\n\\r\\n* Commit some orphaned translations\\r\\n\\r\\n* Lower global timeout to 20000ms\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ef0ee75c3d28c4dbe57d84a2e1323726a9ed7b44\",\"date\":\"2023-09-12T21:49:56+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-2363: Workspace window state should be part of global workspace state (#1339)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Vineet Sharma\",\"authorEmail\":\"sharmava05@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"40074760d4b28c1d895433218ef7eb9ab0387d29\",\"date\":\"2023-03-14T12:47:26-07:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-1492: Remove dangerous global selectors from stylesheets (#1045)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5780de4b34c61446e696646f6bcac9c18957c5fe\",\"date\":\"2023-03-13T11:30:56-07:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove global left nav menu style overrides (#1040)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1cdd2a39d12b4627316bbce72f39ba8e9345f5bb\",\"date\":\"2023-02-28T18:20:00+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-1809: Using global Visit setting to either map Order Encounter to Active Visit (#969)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Configurable option for using visit in order basket\\r\\n\\r\\n* Used the global system setting to either use visit or not\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixed failing tests\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n* Bound mutate function to update orders\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixed failing tests\\r\\n\\r\\n* Test fix\\r\\n\\r\\n* Removed unnecessary variable declaration\",\"authorName\":\"Vineet Sharma\",\"authorEmail\":\"sharmava05@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3450c8bc363e1dca19e36000d034e7c6c5c92e0d\",\"date\":\"2023-01-31T06:35:40-08:00\",\"message\":\"(refactor) Use the bound mutate API instead of global mutate (#964)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5422612cef8b4db6beb7f77587988956d898ee6e\",\"date\":\"2023-01-25T21:35:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix the tooltip UI shown when hovering over long names in the visit header (#954)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fixed the hover state on Full Name\\r\\n\\r\\n* css fixes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fix Tooltip props and the HeaderGlobalAction menu's aria-label\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fix tests\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <julietwamalwa@yahoo.com>\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"cdcb66a2b134d5a7dd372f3e783c99f8ef7d769f\",\"date\":\"2022-08-25T09:56:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix): use hemoglobin (CIEL:21) instead of X-Ray (CIEL:12) by default (#785)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d8625ae097ea65d8c4884ffab37ba47675b23a6c\",\"date\":\"2022-06-27T20:58:39+03:00\",\"message\":\"O3-578: Left Nav Page section is not highlighted correctly. (#721)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Wrap dashboard extension in router.\\r\\nUse location from react-router\\r\\n\\r\\n* Remove the !important and\\r\\nremove the overriding\\r\\nstyles from core\\r\\n\\r\\n* Use global active class\\r\\n\\r\\n* remove duplicate styles for the active global class\",\"authorName\":\"kyampeire Hadijah\",\"authorEmail\":\"30952856+hadijahkyampeire@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"13fb76feb92e07267eb5dc909ae915f99b5d3570\",\"date\":\"2021-11-29T17:59:18+01:00\",\"message\":\"O3-834: Implement Caching of the Offline Forms (#471)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* - Added essential offline forms UI and integrated it into the offline-tools.\\r\\n- Provide stubs/outline for offline caching strategy.\\r\\n\\r\\n* First iteration on the offline forms caching flow: Enable toggles and connect them to the caching logic.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Translation files.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Project restructuring.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Stop registering global cache requests for esm-patient-forms-app and remove requirement for past form encounters as they are used for rendering only.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added explanation for offline code design decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Restored frontend deps and formatted file.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Enhance URLs cached for offline forms. Integrated offline forms into the patient-forms-app module.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Remove debug helpers.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Removed duplicate form entry extension registration.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Updated form caching to leverage SW messaging.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added offline forms overview card to offline tools.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Translations.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Revert esm-form-entry-app package.json changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Removed console.log.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Allow invalidation in useLocalStorage hook.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Revert package.json.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Reinstalled packages.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixed failing tests caused by reinstalling packages.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Remove setupTests from tsconfigs.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Updated yarn.lock.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixed line endings.\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Manu Römer <manuel.roemer@smapiot.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Manu Römer\",\"authorEmail\":\"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d35a27241b16b3932b7aff37f8c15c80f2c202e9\",\"date\":\"2021-09-17T17:02:12+03:00\",\"message\":\"Wrap patient chart in SWRConfig context (#382)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Wrap patient chart in SWRConfig context\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR adds the SWR dependency to the patient chart and wraps the `PatientChart` component in an SWRConfig context that\\r\\nspecifies some sensible global configuration default options for all SWR hooks.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Review feedback\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f995ca12578f7c2cbe58a031816eff2c59386d3\",\"date\":\"2020-02-18T11:25:39+03:00\",\"message\":\"Silence react-i18next warnings when running tests (#121)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Silence react-i8next warning when running tests\\r\\n\\r\\n* Mock the i8next test dependency globally\\r\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":19}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66f1d2b8-3a6c-4f35-8b06-0c1f861e8aaf","uuid":"12aa1475-3ded-488a-84e3-7f7d66620562","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:42:50.103Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"0803b6ebda4a7acf26659df193707d8ad8d68c61\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T12:59:36+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-6026: Prefetch the vitals charts and keep their height while they load (#3727)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Prefetch the vitals charts and keep their height while they load\\n\\nThe vitals and biometrics widgets now start loading their chart code when\\nsomeone hovers over or focuses the table/chart switcher. By the time they\\nclick, the chart chunk is usually ready and the chart renders without a\\nloading state.\\n\\nWhen the chunk isn't ready yet, the fallback is now a SkeletonPlaceholder\\nthe same height as the rendered chart view (466px plus margins) instead of\\na one-line InlineLoading. The spinner shrank the card to a single line and\\npulled the widgets below it up, then pushed them back down when the chart\\nrendered. The skeleton keeps the card at its final height. It keeps\\nrole=\\\"progressbar\\\" and a \\\"Loading\\\" label for screen readers.\\n\\n* Ignore failed chart prefetches\\n\\nThe hover and focus handlers returned the import promise, so a failed\\nchunk download on hover became an unhandled rejection, and O3's global\\nhandler showed an error toast before anyone opened the chart view.\\n\\nThe handlers now call a prefetch wrapper that ignores the failure.\\nReact.lazy still uses the uncaught loader, so opening the chart view\\nretries the download, and a failure there still reaches an error\\nboundary.\\n\\n* Test the chart prefetch in the vitals and biometrics widgets\\n\\nEach widget gets two tests: hovering the table/chart switcher starts\\nloading the chart module, and a failed prefetch leaves the table in\\nplace without an unhandled rejection. Vitest fails the run on an\\nunhandled rejection, so removing the prefetch's catch fails the suite.\\n\\nThe tests mock the chart module with vi.doMock and import a fresh copy\\nof the widget after vi.resetModules, so each test starts with its own\\nReact.lazy state and a chart module that hasn't been imported yet.\\n\\n---------\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"502b0072964465322124ab769a896c3f09aea226\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T18:38:48-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Patient chart shouldn't generate global CSS rules (#3634)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5ba5b70a72d0a60d3dfa6136efe8237ce118d80b\",\"date\":\"2026-06-30T08:26:53+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) Patch OWASP-reported minimatch vulnerabilities (#3433)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Upgrades three pinned minimatch versions to patched releases to fix\\nGHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74, GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26, and GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj\\n(all High severity, 3 CVEs × 3 affected versions = 9 total findings):\\n\\n- minimatch 3.1.2 → 3.1.5  (^3.x requests, e.g. glob, ignore)\\n- minimatch 5.1.0 → 5.1.9  (^5.x requests)\\n- minimatch 9.0.5 → 9.0.9  (^9.x requests)\\n\\nEach upgrade stays within its major version so API compatibility\\nwith dependents is preserved.\",\"authorName\":\"Jayasanka Weerasinghe\",\"authorEmail\":\"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e359da592c220eecde4552ad213e4bc2cdd8e195\",\"date\":\"2025-07-04T09:41:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades (#2554)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades\\n\\nThis PR addresses performance bottlenecks in visit and encounter data management by replacing global revalidation with more targeted cache invalidation.\\n\\nPresently, the global `mutateVisit()` revalidation function triggers 13+ unnecessary network requests per operation, and all visit-related components are revalidated even when only specific data changed.\\n\\nThis approach:\\n\\n- Replaces the global `mutateVisit()` with targeted SWR cache invalidation to reduce 13+ revalidation requests to 1 per operation.\\n- Moves revalidation utilities from the chart app to `@openmrs/esm-patient-common-lib` for better reusability.\\n- Creates multiple utility functions for surgical cache invalidation:\\n  - `invalidateVisitHistory()` - Only invalidates visit history table data\\n  - `invalidatePatientEncounters()` - Only invalidates encounter data\\n  - `invalidateVisitAndEncounterData()` - Combines both for operations affecting both\\n  - `useOptimisticVisitMutations()` - Hook for optimistic updates without network requests\\n- Fixes the encounter table cache invalidation regex to handle flexible URL parameter order.\\n- Updates all visit/encounter operations to use surgical cache targeting:\\n  - Visit creation/editing (`visit-form.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - Visit deletion/restoration (`useDeleteVisit.hook.tsx`)\\n  - Encounter deletion (`encounters-table.component.tsx`)\\n  - Form submissions (`form-entry.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - Visit note creation (`visit-notes-form.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - Order basket operations (`order-basket.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - Vitals/biometrics forms (`vitals-biometrics-form.workspace.tsx`)\\n  - End visit dialog (`end-visit-dialog.component.tsx`)\\n- Preserves current visit component performance by avoiding unnecessary revalidation.\\n- Ensures the `AllEncountersTable` updates correctly after form submissions and other encounter operations.\\n\\nThis eliminates the performance issue where visit CRUD operations triggered excessive network requests returning 304 responses, while maintaining proper data synchronization across all visit and encounter tables.\\n\\n* Make some tweaks and add test coverage\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0458aeea04bfa22b7aa6971a138d90c596232e1c\",\"date\":\"2024-09-05T16:32:39+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Temporarily remove global E2E test timeout\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a8c867fc9ade074fabf84ebcfc7b26f10869dc7b\",\"date\":\"2024-04-06T01:14:40+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Fix Prettier glob patterns\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b3af1a452d58079342c879e09a970b2053f5c46c\",\"date\":\"2024-01-23T22:27:40+02:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-2752: Encounter view UI fixes for RTL languages (#1596)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-2752: encounter view RTL alignment fix\\r\\n\\r\\n* (fix) O3-2752: remove global overrides\\r\\n\\r\\n---------\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Andrey Y <andrey.yakubyshyn@med.me>\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"elimm\",\"authorEmail\":\"elimm@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0a8ebba37f0fc01ba2cd066d45c11a01ae462ade\",\"date\":\"2024-01-10T22:29:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"(refactor) Set global testTimeout in Jest config (#1573)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (refactor) Set global testTimeout in Jest config\\r\\n\\r\\n* Commit some orphaned translations\\r\\n\\r\\n* Lower global timeout to 20000ms\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ef0ee75c3d28c4dbe57d84a2e1323726a9ed7b44\",\"date\":\"2023-09-12T21:49:56+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-2363: Workspace window state should be part of global workspace state (#1339)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Vineet Sharma\",\"authorEmail\":\"sharmava05@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"40074760d4b28c1d895433218ef7eb9ab0387d29\",\"date\":\"2023-03-14T12:47:26-07:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-1492: Remove dangerous global selectors from stylesheets (#1045)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5780de4b34c61446e696646f6bcac9c18957c5fe\",\"date\":\"2023-03-13T11:30:56-07:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove global left nav menu style overrides (#1040)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1cdd2a39d12b4627316bbce72f39ba8e9345f5bb\",\"date\":\"2023-02-28T18:20:00+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-1809: Using global Visit setting to either map Order Encounter to Active Visit (#969)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Configurable option for using visit in order basket\\r\\n\\r\\n* Used the global system setting to either use visit or not\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixed failing tests\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n* Bound mutate function to update orders\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixed failing tests\\r\\n\\r\\n* Test fix\\r\\n\\r\\n* Removed unnecessary variable declaration\",\"authorName\":\"Vineet Sharma\",\"authorEmail\":\"sharmava05@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3450c8bc363e1dca19e36000d034e7c6c5c92e0d\",\"date\":\"2023-01-31T06:35:40-08:00\",\"message\":\"(refactor) Use the bound mutate API instead of global mutate (#964)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5422612cef8b4db6beb7f77587988956d898ee6e\",\"date\":\"2023-01-25T21:35:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix the tooltip UI shown when hovering over long names in the visit header (#954)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fixed the hover state on Full Name\\r\\n\\r\\n* css fixes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fix Tooltip props and the HeaderGlobalAction menu's aria-label\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fix tests\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <julietwamalwa@yahoo.com>\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"cdcb66a2b134d5a7dd372f3e783c99f8ef7d769f\",\"date\":\"2022-08-25T09:56:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix): use hemoglobin (CIEL:21) instead of X-Ray (CIEL:12) by default (#785)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d8625ae097ea65d8c4884ffab37ba47675b23a6c\",\"date\":\"2022-06-27T20:58:39+03:00\",\"message\":\"O3-578: Left Nav Page section is not highlighted correctly. (#721)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Wrap dashboard extension in router.\\r\\nUse location from react-router\\r\\n\\r\\n* Remove the !important and\\r\\nremove the overriding\\r\\nstyles from core\\r\\n\\r\\n* Use global active class\\r\\n\\r\\n* remove duplicate styles for the active global class\",\"authorName\":\"kyampeire Hadijah\",\"authorEmail\":\"30952856+hadijahkyampeire@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"13fb76feb92e07267eb5dc909ae915f99b5d3570\",\"date\":\"2021-11-29T17:59:18+01:00\",\"message\":\"O3-834: Implement Caching of the Offline Forms (#471)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* - Added essential offline forms UI and integrated it into the offline-tools.\\r\\n- Provide stubs/outline for offline caching strategy.\\r\\n\\r\\n* First iteration on the offline forms caching flow: Enable toggles and connect them to the caching logic.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Translation files.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Project restructuring.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Stop registering global cache requests for esm-patient-forms-app and remove requirement for past form encounters as they are used for rendering only.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added explanation for offline code design decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Restored frontend deps and formatted file.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Enhance URLs cached for offline forms. Integrated offline forms into the patient-forms-app module.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Remove debug helpers.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Removed duplicate form entry extension registration.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Updated form caching to leverage SW messaging.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added offline forms overview card to offline tools.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Translations.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Revert esm-form-entry-app package.json changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Removed console.log.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Allow invalidation in useLocalStorage hook.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Revert package.json.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Reinstalled packages.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixed failing tests caused by reinstalling packages.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Remove setupTests from tsconfigs.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Updated yarn.lock.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixed line endings.\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Manu Römer <manuel.roemer@smapiot.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Manu Römer\",\"authorEmail\":\"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d35a27241b16b3932b7aff37f8c15c80f2c202e9\",\"date\":\"2021-09-17T17:02:12+03:00\",\"message\":\"Wrap patient chart in SWRConfig context (#382)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Wrap patient chart in SWRConfig context\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR adds the SWR dependency to the patient chart and wraps the `PatientChart` component in an SWRConfig context that\\r\\nspecifies some sensible global configuration default options for all SWR hooks.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Review feedback\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f995ca12578f7c2cbe58a031816eff2c59386d3\",\"date\":\"2020-02-18T11:25:39+03:00\",\"message\":\"Silence react-i18next warnings when running tests (#121)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Silence react-i8next warning when running tests\\r\\n\\r\\n* Mock the i8next test dependency globally\\r\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":19}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UrsKLyLVReziAQj8XXxRWt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
